The  utility is used to access a Bluetooth Headset with the audio
device.  It opens the device and creates the  control  connection
to the headset, then conducts volume settings each way.  When re‐
ceives  a signal, it will start sending RING codes to the headset
until the headset button is pressed or a signal is received.   If
the  headset is ringing and receives a button press notification,
the specified (if any) is executed.  When the server  channel  is
specified with the option, instead of opening the control connec‐
tion,  will listen on the for incoming connections from the Head‐
set and register as Headset Audio  Gateway  with  the  local  SDP
server.   The options are as follows: Specify an optional command
to be executed when the headset responds to ringing with a button
press event.  This defaults to the contents  of  the  environment
variable,  if set.  Print usage message.  Specify the path to the
mixer device.  This defaults to the contents of  the  environment
variable, or if not set.  Write the PID to so that other programs
can find us later.  This defaults to the contents of the environ‐
ment  variable,  if set.  Register with the local SDP server as a
Headset Audio Gateway and listen for connections on the given RF‐
COMM server channel.  Be verbose.  for Itronix, Inc
